# Commit message (Neubond)

When the user asks for a **commit message**, **write commit message**, **generate commit message**, or runs **`/commit-message`**:

Follow `.cursor/commands/commit-message.md` in full.

Key points:

- Inspect uncommitted work: tracked diffs (`git diff` / staged) **and** untracked paths (`git status`); skim new-file contents when drafting
- Only say nothing to commit when both tracked changes and relevant untracked paths are absent
- Reply with **only** a markdown fenced code block; one concise primary `<type>: <summary>` line inside it
- If multiple distinct themes, add further `<type>: <summary>` lines inside the same block (one per line, no labels)
- Do **not** print bare chat text, `commit message`, `description`, `none`, or `-`
- Do **not** create a git commit unless the user explicitly asks to commit
- Do not mention secrets (`.env` values, tokens, DSN secrets)
